// === PREAMBLE ===
// @trope    Achilles' Heel
// @category Combat Tropes
// @source   https://allthetropes.org/wiki/Achilles%27_Heel
// @domain   Narrative
// @version  1.3
//
// Laconic (per the wiki): any seemingly nigh-invulnerable entity will inevitably have ONE key
// weakness that can and will be exploited — the single weak point that, struck, undoes a foe nothing
// else could touch. Named for Achilles, dipped in the Styx to be invincible save the heel his mother
// held him by. The signature this file recognizes: an entity that is [+Invulnerable] EVERYWHERE save a
// single [+Vulnerable] [+WeakPoint] (often [+Hidden], unknown even to the entity), and a strike aimed
// PRECISELY at that one point — not force against force — that gets through and lays the mighty one low,
// [+Fallen] despite all its power. Rides the action_dynamics Exploit_Weakness -> Finisher chain: the
// strike's kind matches the foe's kind of vulnerability, beating the invulnerability, then the finisher
// lands on the now-[+Exposed] giant. Distinct from David Versus Goliath (which keys on an [+Outmatched]
// underdog as the WHO of the win); here the signature is the entity's own structure — invincible but for
// the one gap — and the deed is the gap being found and struck, by anyone or anything. The weak point is
// the planted Chekhov's Gun of the foe's anatomy: established as the one chink, then fired upon.


// === IMPORTS & ASSOCIATIONS ===
import "trl/concepts/index.trl"            // conflict
import "trl/modules/action_dynamics.trl"   // Exploit_Weakness -> [+Exposed];  Finisher -> [+Defeated]

assoc achilles_heel -> [
  action_dynamics      : "the Exploit_Weakness / Finisher rules of",
  conflict             : "the one weak point decides a",
  david_versus_goliath : "the weaker party wins by hitting the giant's one weak point, an instance of",
  the_worf_effect      : "the established invincible is laid low to make a point, a cousin of",
  chekhovs_gun         : "the weak point is planted as the one chink, then fired upon, like the"
]


// === ONTOLOGY ===
// The pattern is invulnerability defined by its single exception: overwhelming power, but for one gap —
// and the story exists to find and strike that gap. The component cluster is the weak point (Vulnerable)
// inside an otherwise impervious whole (Combat), the chink that fells the mighty (Narrative).
imply AchillesHeel -> [Vulnerable, Combat, WeakPoint, Narrative]


// === ABSTRACT RULE ===
// Recognition: an [+Invulnerable] entity ($mighty) carries exactly one [+Vulnerable] [+WeakPoint],
// keyed to a kind $k; a strike of that very kind finds it (action_dynamics' Exploit_Weakness having
// opened the giant to [+Exposed], because a kind-matched strike beats any guard — here, beats the
// invulnerability), and a finisher lands. The deed IS an Achilles' Heel: the mighty one is [+Fallen]
// despite its power, undone not by greater force but by the single gap in it. The [+Invulnerable] +
// lone-[+WeakPoint] structure on the foe is the whole signature — strike a merely-tough foe anywhere and
// this does not fire; strike the one chink in the impervious and the giant falls. Tags the felling deed.
rule AchillesHeel {
  when:
    char $mighty [+Invulnerable] [+WeakPoint] [+Vulnerable(to=$k)] [+Exposed]
    evt  $f [&Finishes(agent=$striker, target=$mighty)]
  then:
    $f [+AchillesHeel]
    $mighty [+Fallen]
}


// === CONCRETE VIGNETTE: The War of the Worlds (H. G. Wells, novel, 1898) ===
// The Martians come in their fighting-machines and lay England waste. No human weapon touches them:
// the Heat-Ray and Black Smoke break every army sent against them; artillery, navy, and rifle alike are
// useless — they are, to all of humanity's force, invulnerable. But the invaders carry one weak point
// none of them know they have, hidden in their very biology: arriving from a sterilized Mars, they have
// no immunity to Earth's bacteria. The microbes — the humblest things on the planet, against which not a
// shot is fired — find that one gap. The conquerors, untouched by all our power, are laid low in their
// machines by the common cold; the tripods stand silent. The invincible invasion falls, not to a hero's
// strike but to the single biological chink in an otherwise impervious foe.

// THE MARTIANS (the invaders in their fighting-machines — invulnerable to every human weapon)
char martians [+Antagonist] [+Invulnerable]
// the one gap, hidden in their biology: no immunity to Earth's microbes — unknown even to them
martians [+WeakPoint]
martians [+Vulnerable(to="Microbes")]
// THE EARTH BACTERIA (the humblest agent — the strike no army could land, aimed at the one weak point)
char bacteria [+Common]
// THE MARTIAN FIGHTING-MACHINE (the tripod — power that nothing human can touch)
obj tripod [+Conspicuous]
// EXT. THE RUINED OUTSKIRTS OF LONDON - DAY (the silenced machines, the red weed dying back)
set london [+Exterior] [+Day]

scene the_red_weed {
  beat 1 {
    martians @ london
    bacteria @ london
    // the microbes reach the one gap — a strike of the kind the Martians have no defence against;
    // action_dynamics' Exploit_Weakness fires (kind="Microbes" matches Vulnerable(to="Microbes")),
    // deriving martians [+Exposed] — the invulnerability beaten at its single weak point.
    evt the_infection [&Strikes(agent=bacteria, target=martians, kind="Microbes")]
  }
  beat 2 {
    // the finish: the conquerors die in their machines — the tripods stand silent over a saved Earth.
    evt the_silence [&Finishes(agent=bacteria, target=martians)]
    // Finisher -> martians [+Defeated];  AchillesHeel tags the deed, martians [+Fallen] despite all power.
  }
}
